FULL SALES LIFECYCLE
From New Lead → Active Paying Client

PHASE 1 — Lead Capture & Entry
🎯 Trigger
A new prospect shows interest (form, call, referral, campaign, manual entry).

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 1: Create New Lead
Navigate to CRM → Leads
Click “Create Lead”
Input:
Lead Name
Company
Email
Phone
Source (campaign, referral, website, etc.)
Assigned Sales Rep
Save
System Behavior:
Lead appears in Lead List
Status = New
Timestamp recorded
Assigned rep receives notification (if enabled)

Track B — Customer Experience
Prospect submits inquiry or speaks to rep.
May receive:
Auto confirmation email
Thank you message
Enters company database.
Emotional state:
Curious. Evaluating options.

PHASE 2 — Lead Qualification
🎯 Goal
Determine if lead is worth pursuing.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 2: Review Lead Details
Open lead profile
Check:
Source
Budget indicators
Notes
Communication history
Step 3: First Contact
Log a call
Send email
Schedule meeting
Add notes
System records:
Call logs
Email interactions
Meeting schedule
Activity timeline
Step 4: Update Lead Status
Change status to:
Contacted
Qualified
Not Qualified
Follow-up Required
Decision Gate:
If not qualified → mark as lost.
If qualified → proceed to conversion.

Track B — Customer Experience
Receives outreach (call/email).
Books demo or meeting.
Explains needs and expectations.
Emotional state:
Testing credibility. Comparing alternatives.

PHASE 3 — Lead Conversion
🎯 Goal
Convert qualified lead into structured CRM entities.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 5: Convert Lead
Click “Convert Lead”
System auto-creates:
Account (Company)
Contact (Person)
Opportunity (Revenue potential)
Lead record becomes:
Converted
Linked to new entities
Now managed inside Opportunity Pipeline.

Track B — Customer Experience
After demo/meeting, prospect signals interest.
Discussion moves toward proposal stage.
Emotional state:
Interested but cautious.

PHASE 4 — Opportunity & Pipeline Management
🎯 Goal
Move deal through sales stages.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 6: Manage Opportunity
Inside Opportunity:
Set:
Expected Revenue
Close Date
Stage (e.g., Proposal, Negotiation)
Probability %
Step 7: Move Through Pipeline Stages
Stages typically:
Qualification
Proposal
Negotiation
Decision
Closed Won / Closed Lost
System tracks:
Stage changes
Value forecasting
Pipeline analytics
Step 8: Add Activities
Schedule follow-up calls
Attach proposal files
Log meetings
Add internal notes

Track B — Customer Experience
Receives:
Proposal document
Pricing breakdown
Product demo follow-ups
Negotiates scope or pricing.
Emotional state:
Evaluating risk vs reward.

PHASE 5 — Quotation
🎯 Goal
Formalize offer.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 9: Create Quote
Navigate to Quotes → Create
Select:
Account
Contact
Products/services
Quantity
Tax
Discounts
System:
Calculates totals
Generates quote document
Sets status = Draft
Step 10: Send Quote
Change status to Sent
Email directly from system
Quote statuses:
Draft
Sent
Accepted
Declined

Track B — Customer Experience
Receives official quote.
Reviews pricing and scope.
Approves or requests revisions.
Emotional state:
Decision-making moment.

PHASE 6 — Order Creation
🎯 Trigger
Quote is accepted.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 11: Convert Quote to Sales Order
Click “Convert to Order”
System:
Creates Sales Order
Pulls data from quote
Links to Account & Opportunity
Order status:
Pending
Confirmed
Processing
Completed

Track B — Customer Experience
Receives order confirmation.
Expects service or product delivery timeline.
Emotional state:
Expectation of fulfillment.

PHASE 7 — Invoice & Payment
🎯 Goal
Monetize the deal.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 12: Generate Invoice
From Sales Order → Create Invoice
Invoice includes:
Line items
Taxes
Payment terms
Due date
Status:
Draft
Sent
Paid
Partially Paid
Overdue
Step 13: Record Payment
Log payment method
Update invoice status
System updates:
Revenue tracking
Financial reports
Account history

Track B — Customer Experience
Receives invoice.
Pays via supported payment method.
Gets payment confirmation.
Emotional state:
Commitment achieved.

PHASE 8 — Become Active Client
🎯 Trigger
Invoice paid.

Track A — Sales Rep Journey
Step 14: Opportunity Status = Closed Won
System:
Updates revenue reports
Reflects win rate
Updates pipeline metrics
Step 15: Account Lifecycle Status = Active Client
Now the account:
Can have projects
Can receive campaigns
Can generate recurring invoices
Can enter customer success workflows

Track B — Customer Experience
Onboarding begins.
May receive:
Welcome email
Project kickoff
Support access
Dedicated account manager
Emotional state:
Transition from buyer → partner.

END STATE
In CRM:
Lead → Converted
Account → Active
Opportunity → Closed Won
Sales Order → Completed
Invoice → Paid

SYSTEM TOUCHPOINT SUMMARY
Stage
Primary Module Used
Lead Entry
Leads
Qualification
Leads + Activities
Conversion
